{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-curvature-rank","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:curvature-rank","kind":"definition","title":"Curvature-rank $r(T_w)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hecke-curvature-2-cocycle"],"cites":["references/bokutchen2014"],"tags":["curvature-rank","gb-filtration","normal-form","hecke","reduction"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.WedderburnMass.curvatureRank","text":"curvature-rank.md","leanSource":"curvature-rank.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"def:curvature-rank\"></a>\n<strong>Definition.</strong> <em>Curvature-rank <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r(T_w)</code></em></p>\n<p><strong>Definition (curvature-rank).</strong>\n<em>The curvature-rank <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r(T_w)</code> is the smallest non-negative integer <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r</code> mapping the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r</code>-fold iterated curvature <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F^{\\,r}(T_w)</code> into the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^{\\,r}(q) \\setminus J^{\\,r+1}(q)</code> filtration stratum. It counts the minimal number of reduction steps required to drive <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_w</code> into normal form.</em></p>\n"}
